{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{X}' \\ar[r] \\ar[d]_{f'} & \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n\\mathcal{Y}' \\ar[r]^g & \\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Mor(\\Spec(k), \\mathcal{X}')\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Mor(\\Spec(k), \\mathcal{Y}') \\times \\Mor(\\Spec(k), \\mathcal{X})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$k$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-identify-automorphism-groups}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stabilizer-preserving-points-cartesian}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:96226cc50e4753576657aeaea35a3d0be06b5a410a265f5c165efa41ca122667", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e4fae39dfddcd46922f8d8b8a35accc2705d3af2506eb87cd19d1608c759a3a7", "source_text": "Let\n<MATH_0001>\nbe a cartesian diagram of algebraic stacks. If <MATH_0002> induces an isomorphism\nbetween automorphism groups at points\n(Remark <REF_0001>),\nthen\n<MATH_0003>\nis injective on isomorphism classes for any field <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a8dc41c27e247fbad881f48dff4187991fcb9978fa5c4db7752fa074a9c6a427", "unit_id": "tag:0DUC:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(y', x)$", "MATH_0002": "$x'$", "MATH_0003": "$2$", "MATH_0004": "$x'$", "MATH_0005": "$(x, y', \\alpha)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\alpha : g \\circ y' \\to f \\circ x$", "MATH_0007": "$2$", "MATH_0008": "$(x, y', \\beta)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0010": "$\\beta$", "MATH_0011": "$k$", "MATH_0012": "$\\epsilon$", "MATH_0013": "$G_{f(x)}$", "MATH_0014": "$f$", "MATH_0015": "$G_x \\to G_{f(x)}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\epsilon$", "MATH_0017": "$k$", "MATH_0018": "$\\gamma$", "MATH_0019": "$G_x$", "MATH_0020": "$(\\gamma, \\text{id}) : (x, y', \\alpha) \\to\n(x, y', \\beta)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a9ec0164cbcf94a5e7cd98a09a3121a24d652f864c00b6542f83940471d85090", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:280e5f907aab53d6eb3ed75c07db41c53ad4220582d82996fd3b5109cbbb5643", "source_text": "We have to show that given <MATH_0001> there is at most one <MATH_0002>\nmapping to it.\nBy our construction of <MATH_0003>-fibre products, a morphism\n<MATH_0004> is given by a triple <MATH_0005>\nwhere  <MATH_0006> is a <MATH_0007>-morphism.\nNow, suppose we have a second such triple <MATH_0008>.\nThen <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010> differ by a <MATH_0011>-valued point\n<MATH_0012> of the automorphism group algebraic space <MATH_0013>.\nSince <MATH_0014> induces an isomorphism <MATH_0015> by\nassumption, this means we can lift <MATH_0016> to a <MATH_0017>-valued point\n<MATH_0018> of <MATH_0019>. Then <MATH_0020> is an isomorphism as desired.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c8e441bd441234d2280ac01ab7643ad96635f841405f91bb532227d4d0b879e0", "unit_id": "tag:0DUC:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0DU6", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$k$", "MATH_0005": "$$\nf : \\Mor(\\Spec(k), \\mathcal{X}) \\longrightarrow \\Mor(\\Spec(k), \\mathcal{Y})\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-identify-automorphism-groups}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-etale-iso}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:834a5477a631d343fc7e801130bbb27d352ca3c43b8eb6b35d1f4a9e4dbbef59", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:022542dfbefe0d67b2b626b3f627d5d41452c2a609cee06149d1b982185a88a2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nAssume <MATH_0002> is <ACCENT_0001>tale, <MATH_0003> induces an isomorphism\nbetween automorphism groups at points\n(Remark <REF_0001>),\nand for every algebraically closed field <MATH_0004> the functor\n<MATH_0005>\nis an equivalence. Then <MATH_0006> is an isomorphism.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2f4750f6eec2927e0d6c9186988ecbca400850467a90447767bf0709c7d0651a", "unit_id": "tag:0DUD:statement"}
